# Rottenmouth Viper: "As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may sacrifice any number of nonland permanents. This
# spell costs {1} less to cast for each permanent sacrificed this way." How many is announced as it is cast (CR 601.2b) and
# the total cost determined with it (CR 601.2f, 118.7a): sacrificing three Ornithopters, its {5}{B} costs {2}{B}, which the
# three Swamps' {B}{B}{B} pays exactly. A land is not among what may be sacrificed. It enters, a blight counter is put on it,
# and for its one counter Bot2 (with only cards in hand, no nonland permanent) chooses to lose 4 life. The number sacrificed
# is no X (its mana cost has none, CR 107.3): the Viper has no X and its mana value is its mana cost's, 6 (CR 202.3).

